<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>netstandard2.0</TargetFramework>
    <LangVersion>latest</LangVersion>
    <Deterministic>true</Deterministic>
    <GenerateAssemblyInfo>false</GenerateAssemblyInfo>

    <!-- 1. Configure NuGet Package generation and XML Documentation -->
    <GeneratePackageOnBuild>true</GeneratePackageOnBuild>
    <GenerateDocumentationFile>true</GenerateDocumentationFile>
        
    <!-- 2. NuGet Package Metadata Info -->
    <PackageId>GeometryHelper.ArrangeAlgorithms</PackageId>
    <Version>3.0.0</Version>
    <Authors>Nguyen Thang</Authors>
    <Company>Nguyen Thang</Company>
    <Description>A 2D label placement library for engineering drawings that automatically arranges labels to prevent overlaps with each other and blocked regions. Features 5 layout algorithms: Greedy, Bounded Backtracking, Simulated Annealing, Force-Directed, and Constraint Satisfaction. The geometry it works in comes from the GeometryHelper.PlaneGeometry package, which arrives as a dependency.</Description>
    <PackageProjectUrl>https://github.com/nguyenthanguth/GeometryHelper</PackageProjectUrl>
    <RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/nguyenthanguth/GeometryHelper</RepositoryUrl>
    <RepositoryType>git</RepositoryType>
    <PackageLicenseExpression>MIT</PackageLicenseExpression>
    <PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>
    <PackageIcon>icon.png</PackageIcon>
    <Copyright>Copyright © 2026 Nguyen Thang</Copyright>
    <PackageTags>label-placement geometry cad autocad tekla algorithm greedy backtracking simulated-annealing force-directed csp</PackageTags>
    <PackageReleaseNotes>

      2D label placement for engineering drawings. Given labels that each carry a guide segment and a
      set of blocked regions, the library returns the translation vectors that keep the labels off each
      other and off the blocked regions.

      - Five algorithms behind one entry point, chosen through ArrangeOptions.Algorithm: Greedy,
        Bounded Backtracking, Simulated Annealing, Force-Directed and Constraint Satisfaction.
      - Arrange.Run fills in a translation for every label; a label that cannot be improved keeps a
        zero vector rather than being dropped from the result.
      - Blocked regions accept both polygons and lines, so dimensions and the rebar centrelines a mark
        must not cross are expressed the same way.
      - Offsets, spacing, iteration counts and the tolerance are all set through ArrangeOptions, whose
        defaults are in millimetres to match conventional structural drawings.
      - It depends on AutoCAD and Tekla for nothing. The geometry comes from
        GeometryHelper.PlaneGeometry, which arrives as a dependency along with
        GeometryHelper.CommonGeometry.
    </PackageReleaseNotes>

    <!-- 3. Embed source code and Debug symbols into DLL to support F12 original code viewing -->
    <DebugType>embedded</DebugType>
    <EmbedAllSources>true</EmbedAllSources>
    <GenerateDependencyFile>false</GenerateDependencyFile>

  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\GeometryHelper.PlaneGeometry\GeometryHelper.PlaneGeometry.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <None Include="README.md" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
    <None Include="icon.png" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>